%S A123450 1,2,4,11,33,148,906,8887,136755,3269254,115811790,5855491708,
%T A123450 410579742681
%N A123450 Number of preperfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123450 A vertex x predominates a distinct vertex y if either xy is an edge and every maximum clique containing y contains x, or xy is a nonedge and every maximum independent set containing x contains y. A graph is preperfect if every induced subgraph with at least two vertices has a predomination pair. All preperfect graphs are perfect. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 14 2026
